(:id "port/python/vt/id-table-wire" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/pythontable/vtidtable_rows_test.go: TestPythonVtIdtableRows (the twelve manifest cases luatable's vtcells_test.go names for the row: vocab_wide, vocab_low, peer_a, peer_b, vocab9_wide, vocab9_low, login_full, match_full, escape_unnamed_field, escape_named_field, escape_element, nopayload_named_field)" "internal/codegen/pythontable/vtidtable_rows_test.go: TestPythonVtIdtableRowsNegativeControl/save-layout-hash, /load-record-hash, /accept-held-escape (each fault planted in a COPY of the emitted runtime)" "internal/codegen/pythontable/idtable_test.go: TestPythonVtIdtable, TestPythonVtIdtableNegativeControl" "make python-vt-idtable-rows python-vt-idtable-rows-negative-control (make/python-vt-idtable-rows.mk); make/negative-controls.d/python-vt-idtable-rows-negative-control.json") :tested-revision "1eebddd5854313717f743bb1ee6a19a7eaf674cc" :note "2026-11-17: every manifest case of the id-table-wire row runs through the one read under both pinned interpreters (CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2, staged by make dist-python), and the two agree. The eight instances are fixed roots, read and written as form 3 as luatable reads them through ReadFixed: each loads, saves back byte-identical and measures its length. The four report rows answer the Go engine: the plain load refuses previous_form as Decode does, and the variable reader answers DecodeVariable's verdict on the same bytes (2026-11-22, R17: kind 31 is held by name and never written, so escape_unnamed_field, escape_named_field and escape_element refuse wire_damaged; nopayload_named_field refuses kind_mismatch). The negative control turns every instance case red with the fixed save's layout hash one bit off and with the fixed read's record-hash test inverted, and escape_unnamed_field red when the variable read skips an unnamed kind 31 by its L as the removed escape did. No runtime change was needed. Run on macOS arm64 with SCHEMA_SLOW=1 at this revision.")
